#definition[The centaliser of a subset][
Let $G$ be a group and $A subset.eq G$

The centraliser of $A$ is the set $C_G (A) = {g in G: g a g^(-1)=a forall a in A} = {g in G : g a = a g forall a in A}$  
]

#definition([Normalizer of a group],[
Let $G $ be a group and $A subset.eq G$

For $g in G$ define $g A g^(-1) = {g a g^(-1): a in A}$

The normaliser of $A$ in $G$ is defined as $N_G (A) = {g in G: g A g^(-1) = A}$   
])

