#prob[Prove that if $x $ is the only element of order 2 in a group, then $x $ lies in the centre of the group][

Let $x in G$ where $G $ is a group and asume that that $x^2 = 1$  

Note that for all $g in G$  the element $g x g^(-1)$ also has order 2 since $(g x g^(-1)) (g x g^(-1)) = g x g^(-1) g x g^(-1) = e$

By assumption, this means ($forall g$ )that $x = g x g^(-1) arrow.double x g = g x$ i.e. that $x$ is in the center of $G $ 

$qed$ 

]
